Permission allow rule (../../../.claude/settings.json): Write(.claude/**) is not matched by file permission checks — only Edit(path) rules are. Use Edit(.claude/**) instead (Edit rules cover all file-editing tools).
Two things were missing: the group never exposed `aria-invalid`/`aria-required`, and the error text wasn't associated with the group — so the only signal was a visual `error` attribute plus a live region that only fires when `error` is set (not for `valueMissing`).

## `updated()`

```js
  get isInvalid() {
    return Boolean(this.error) || (this.validity && this.validity !== 'valid');
  }

  // this.error covers customError; valueMissing has no consumer-supplied text
  get errorMessage() {
    if (this.error) return this.error;
    if (this.validity === 'valueMissing') return 'Select an option.';
    return '';
  }

  updated(changedProperties) {
    if (changedProperties.has('error') || changedProperties.has('validity')) {
      const invalid = this.isInvalid;

      this.items.forEach((el) => {
        // existing behaviour: mirror the error attribute onto each child
        if (this.error) el.setAttribute('error', '');
        else el.removeAttribute('error');

        // each radio is individually focusable, so each carries the state
        if (invalid) el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');
        else el.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
      });
    }
  }
```

## `render()`

```js
  render() {
    const invalid = this.isInvalid;
    const message = this.errorMessage;

    return html`
      <fieldset
        role="radiogroup"
        aria-required="${this.required ? 'true' : 'false'}"
        aria-invalid="${invalid ? 'true' : 'false'}"
        aria-describedby="${ifDefined(message ? 'error-message' : undefined)}">
        <legend><slot name="legend"></slot></legend>
        <slot></slot>
        <p id="error-message" role="alert">${message}</p>
      </fieldset>
    `;
  }
```

Requires `import { ifDefined } from 'lit/directives/if-defined.js';`.

What changed and why:

- **`aria-invalid` on the group and on each radio.** Screen readers announce the focused radio, not the container, so the per-child mirroring in `updated()` is what makes the state audible while arrowing through options. The group-level attribute covers AT that reports the radiogroup on entry.
- **`aria-describedby` → the message.** The slotted radios flatten into the `<fieldset>` in the accessibility tree, so a description on the group is announced when entering it. Note this only works because the message lives in the same (shadow) tree as the `<fieldset>` — `aria-describedby` on the light-DOM radios could not have referenced it.
- **The live region is always rendered**, with text swapped in rather than the whole `<p>` being created. Several screen readers miss a `role="alert"` node that is inserted into the DOM at the same moment it gets content; an existing empty region that later fills reliably announces. Dropped `aria-live="assertive"` — `role="alert"` already implies it.
- **`updated()` now watches `validity`,** not just `error`. Previously a `valueMissing` state changed nothing at all in the DOM.
- **`aria-required`** so the constraint is known before the user trips it, rather than only after.

One assumption worth your review: I added a default `'Select an option.'` string for `valueMissing`, since that validity state has no consumer-supplied text and would otherwise be flagged invalid with nothing to describe it. If your design system routes that copy through a token or a `setCustomValidity`-style API, swap the getter to read from there.
